* Cascaded JFET Overdrive — exported from Lutherie
* Three JFET gain stages in a row, laid out like the preamp of a valve amp. JFETs clip softly and unevenly much as triodes do, so this gives amp-like overdrive at 9 V.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 1k
CC1 IN N2 22n
RR1 N2 0 1Meg
JJ1 N3 N2 N4 J_J201
RR2 VCC_9V N3 33k
RR3 N4 0 1k
CC2 N4 0 10u
CC3 N3 N6 22n
* Gain pot 500k A taper at 60%
RVR1a 0 N7 81k
RVR1b N7 N6 419k
JJ2 N8 N7 N9 J_J201
RR4 VCC_9V N8 33k
RR5 N9 0 1k
CC4 N8 N10 22n
RR6 N10 N11 470k
RR7 N11 0 470k
JJ3 N12 N11 N13 J_J201
RR8 VCC_9V N12 33k
RR9 N13 0 1k
CC5 N13 0 1u
CC6 N12 N14 100n
CC7 N14 N15 10n
* Tone pot 50k B taper at 50%
RVR2a N15 0 25k
RVR2b 0 0 25k
* Level pot 100k A taper at 60%
RVR3a 0 OUT 16.2k
RVR3b OUT N14 83.8k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg
VVS2 VCC_9V 0 DC 9.0

.model J_J201 NJF(Beta=0.001304 Vto=-0.5 Lambda=0.0125 Cgs=4e-12 Cgd=4e-12)

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata cascaded_jfet_overdrive.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end